          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.fact",
          "value": {
            "status": "active",
            "summary": "Namarra — kingdom of a thousand channels. Land and livelihood: rice, grain, flax, dates, fish, salt, reeds, saffron, canal transport, Rule: King Javed II relies on canal councils, temple granaries, tax flotillas, and village Character: fast negotiation, layered hospitality, satirical puppetry, boat races, and a Magic: river blessings and protective marks are common culture; reliable magic is scarce and Old wound: Sundering-era refugees founded settlements never formally recognized by the Crown. Current pressure: several living villages have vanished from royal records while their crops",
            "provenance": "Caldris world bible — polity dossiers",
