          "value": {
            "status": "active",
            "summary": "Seven Lamps League — cities that agree commercially. Land and livelihood: three major ports and four smaller member cities around the Lantern Rule: rotating civic chair, member councils, merchant courts, dock assemblies, and enough Character: multilingual streets, professional hospitality, public satire, practical Magic: the League regulates magical services as trades while banning several forms of Old wound: Aster Quay hosted the final Concord negotiations and may have helped the last High Current pressure: the rotating Chair, Ansel Daro, vanished with a key to a sealed archive and",
